As ascensions go this was a pretty crappy one, but I thought I'd do a
YAAP anyway for a few reasons - it's been five years since the last,
it's the first time I've ever died then gone on to ascend, it's the
first time I've ascended on nethack.alt.org, and I think it's the
first time I've ever beaten Demogorgon.

Aside from that things were pretty unremarkable - the highlights were
probably getting a wish from a throne (which went on GDSM) and keeping
an ogre (etc.) as a pet for quite some time. Oh, and a bones file on
the first level of the Mines with Excalibur and a master mind flayer.
Luckily I had just managed to get a wand of fire, and the ghost was
helpfully keeping us apart. :-) I actually ended up using Excalibur
for the whole game, it was decent enough for a long time but I really
should have tried to get something better towards the end.

Anyway, about that Demogorgon encounter. This was on dlvl 38 on my way
up with the Amulet, he appeared seemingly out of nowhere. I was lucky
enough to get a few hits in without any response *and* safely climb up
the stairs to Vlad's place - then failed to realise just how lucky
that had been and came straight back down to get to the real upstairs.
Unsurprisingly Demogorgon soon teleported to meet me, and within a few
moves I was quaffing my sorely limited supply of holy water and still
being stupid enough to try just beating him to death. Worse yet, I was
suddenly burdened (I'm not sure how this happened) but didn't drop my
bag.

Within a few moves he'd summoned a succubus and Yeenoghu. That's when
I had my first bright idea, to dig a hole and fall through. Which left
me on dlvl 39 with those two, but no sign of D. I hit Yeenoghu, giving
the succubus time to do the obvious, and dlvl 39 just happens to be
the top level of the Wizard's tower so she can't even teleport away.
Before I get another turn, D appears and kills me. One "oLS later, the
situation is grim - HP back at max, but all three of them still right
next to me, AC down to -10 and no magic resistance or cancellation,
and still deathly sick and burdened.

At this point I start getting the idea a bit, and zap D to teleport
him away at least for a second. The succubus has another go, leaving
my AC down to 6 and the game struggling to fit my status in with "Conf
Ill Stun Burd". I zap D away again, but still burdened and without my
speed boots on I don't even get a move before he's back again and
takes me right down to 1 hit point. (!) *Finally* I do what I should
have done when I first saw him and engrave the E-word with a wand of
fire. I put on my spare "oLS and at long last, drop my bag. Then I do
what should have been my second move originally, to use the spare
non-wrest wish from the castle wand on a cockatrice corpse and start
bashing. Once things settled down, I soon got unburdened by dropping
all my gold.

After that little drama, the rest of the game went a bit more
smoothly. The Astral Plane was a bit scary at times because I never
used a ring of conflict, and my max HP was only about 200 and my AC
about -30 - no further chatting-to-priests was possible after losing
all that gold, and I was a bit paranoid about taking armour off to
enchant anything in case the Wizard showed up. But luckily there was
plenty of insect-summoning going on and I had a few wands of death to
hand, and Crom's was the first altar I checked.


